<title>AUSTRALIA: SFE wheat steady on SYCOM after heavy hedging play.</title>
<headline>SFE wheat steady on SYCOM after heavy hedging play.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) wheat futures traded steady on Monday through the SYCOM electronic system, with floor trading closed for a New South Wales bank holiday.</p>
<p>January 1998 sold 22 lots at a steady A$195.00 on SYCOM.</p>
<p>This followed heavy trading on SYCOM on Friday night when more than 100 wheat put options traded.</p>
<p>The options trade was based on hedging to guard against a falling market, brokers said.  </p>
